<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhana Nanda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 321 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhana Nanda was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty">Nanda dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Greek accounts of Alexander's campaign speak of the great army of the eastern king, which helped turn Alexander's troops back at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a> in 326 BCE. Indian traditions remember him as greedy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya">Chandragupta Maurya</a> overthrew him around 322 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhana-nanda.jpg" alt="Dhana Nanda" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avantiputra7 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanda_Empire,_c.325_BCE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
